Subject: control mode, look at the state every 4 ms

The control thread wakes up to say where the player is. At 33 ms the end of the
file was reported up to 33 ms late, and a program that chains files starts the
next one on that report: the gap between two files varied by that much. At 4 ms it
varies by at most that, at no measurable cost.
--- a/cmd/rju-play.c
+++ b/cmd/rju-play.c
@@ -588,7 +588,8 @@
 	report_init(&rs);
 	while (!stopping(d)) {
 		struct pollfd p = { 0, POLLIN, 0 };
-		int r = poll(&p, 1, 33);
+		/* Short: this loop also reports the end of the file, and the program that chains files starts the next one on it. */
+		int r = poll(&p, 1, 4);
 		if (r > 0 && (p.revents & (POLLIN | POLLHUP))) {
 			ssize_t n = read(0, buf + fill, sizeof(buf) - fill - 1);
 			if (n <= 0) {
